#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0097 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "DISCRIMINATING (finding AD0097-F1, M2-Q1 pin). An OCCURRENCE dataset is OUTSIDE the sheet's 'BDS, ADNCA, MDBDS, ADAMOTHER' list, but Scope.Domains.Include: [ALL] admits it, so the rule executes and fires. This fixture asserts the scope as SHIPPED. If the M2-Q1 lane narrows the Scope, this is the one fixture that must be re-authored (to expect=skipped) - it is named in finding AD0097-F1 for exactly that reason. Its mirror image is PMDA-AD0111-skipped_occds_structure-ADAE. ESCALATE, do not rewrite, if this lands otherwise."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 TRTPG1N=1
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AEDECOD type=Char
col TRTPG1N type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | 1
